2.
Definitions.
- In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(i)
"Act" means the Merchant Shipping Act, 1958 (
44 of 1958
);
(ii)
"compartment" means a hold, or cargo space bounded by bulkheads at each end and having decks above and below;
(iii)
"feeders" means feeders constructed in accordance with the requirements specified in the First Schedule;
(iv)
"grain" includes wheat, maize or corn, oats, rye, barley, rice, pulses and seeds;
(v)
"metacentric height" means the distance between the transverse metacentre (M) and the centre of gravity (G) corrected
for the free surface effects of liquids in tanks, and for the purposes of rule 5, for the free surface effects of grain in
feeders;
(vi)
"Schedule" means a Schedule to these rules;
(vii)
"shifting boards" means shifting boards constructed in accordance with the requirements specified in the Second
Schedule;
(viii)
"shores" means shores conforming to the requirements specified in the Third Schedule;
(ix)
"stays" means stays the fitting of which conforms to requirements of the Fourth Schedule;
(x)
"upright" means upright, the fitting of which conforms to the requirements of the Fifth Schedule.
